  "flow": {
    "kind": "sequence",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "prepare",
        "kind": "call",
        "operation": "prepare_source",
        "arguments": {
          "argv": {
            "ref": "inputs.argv"
          },
          "context": {
            "ref": "inputs.context"
          }
        },
        "description": "scripts/recursive_goal_tools.py checks mutation permission, native hub preflight and declared writes. Native prepare_source validates case_id prefix and nonempty question/answer, writes source text, runs extraction -> informal expansion -> readiness review, and packs original record, paths, interpreter, stage reports, settings, empty repair paths and seven pending physics stages."
      },
      {
        "id": "physics",
        "kind": "loop",
        "description": "PHYSICS_STAGES order: symbol_table -> equation_parse -> dimension_model -> unit_grounding -> law_grounding -> gap_detection -> derivation_plan. Each call uses source_text and output paths, records its report and pops one pending entry even on recorded failure. The wrapper returns done = not pending. Seven starts nonempty and exits normally at seven; exhaustion signaling is unreachable for the native queue.",
        "state_type": "State",
        "initial": {
          "ref": "steps.prepare.outputs.state"
        },
        "body": {
          "kind": "call",
          "operation": "visit_physics_stage",
          "arguments": {
            "state": {
              "ref": "loop.state"
            },
            "context": {
              "ref": "inputs.context"
            }
          }
        },
        "next_state": {
          "ref": "body.outputs.state"
        },
        "until": {
          "ref": "body.outputs.done"
        },
        "max_iterations": 7,
        "on_exhausted": "fail",
        "outputs": {
          "state": {
            "type": "State",
            "value": {
              "ref": "loop.state"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "critique",
        "kind": "call",
        "operation": "plan_critique_ground",
        "arguments": {
          "state": {
            "ref": "steps.physics.outputs.state"
          },
          "context": {
            "ref": "inputs.context"
          }
        },
        "description": "Native ordered block: lean_workflow_plan -> lean_type_packet -> lean_assumption_packet -> background_plan -> unit_report -> semantics_critic -> assumption_critic -> dimension_critic -> drift_monitor -> math_object_detection -> workbench_plan -> mathlib_grounding. Source, existing Lean, type/assumption/expansion packets and earlier reports feed later calls. Then pack four repair names into pending and reset repair_plan_paths."
      },
      {
        "id": "repairs",
        "kind": "loop",
        "description": "REPAIR_STAGES order: notational_collapse_repair -> abstraction_elevation_repair -> proof_strategy_alignment_repair -> implicit_premise_normalization. Each consumes drift/object/workbench paths, records its stage, appends the output path in order and pops pending; wrapper computes done. Fourth exits normally even with recorded failures; native empty-queue invocation raises ValueError, not another iteration.",
        "state_type": "State",
        "initial": {
          "ref": "steps.critique.outputs.state"
        },
        "body": {
          "kind": "call",
          "operation": "visit_repair_plan",
          "arguments": {
            "state": {
              "ref": "loop.state"
            },
            "context": {
              "ref": "inputs.context"
            }
          }
        },
        "next_state": {
          "ref": "body.outputs.state"
        },
        "until": {
          "ref": "body.outputs.done"
        },
        "max_iterations": 4,
        "on_exhausted": "fail",
        "outputs": {
          "state": {
            "type": "State",
            "value": {
              "ref": "loop.state"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "plans",
        "kind": "call",
        "operation": "finish_plans",
        "arguments": {
          "state": {
            "ref": "steps.repairs.outputs.state"
          },
          "context": {
            "ref": "inputs.context"
          }
        },
        "description": "Ordered block: pathology_repair -> generative_repair -> generative_critic -> repair_expansion_map -> recursive_control -> final_hypothesis_review. Ordered repair paths feed pathology/generative/expansion plans; source, existing Lean, packets and prior outputs supply dependencies. Controller receives unchanged iteration/max_iterations, no previous maps; it only plans complete/recurse/blocked. No frontier execution, iteration increment or target Lean edits."
      },
      {
        "id": "compile",
        "kind": "call",
        "operation": "compile_interpret",
        "arguments": {
          "state": {
            "ref": "steps.plans.outputs.state"
          },
          "context": {
            "ref": "inputs.context"
          }
        },
        "description": "Run lake env lean on the existing Lean file without local timeout; save combined stdout/stderr as lean_execution_raw.log, record compiler success, then run diagnostic interpreter. Pack compiler evidence and compute silent_success = compiler returncode zero AND stripped raw log empty."
      },
      {
        "id": "evidence",
        "kind": "switch",
        "cases": [
          {
            "id": "silent_success",
            "when": {
              "ref": "steps.compile.outputs.silent_success"
            },
            "body": {
              "kind": "call",
              "operation": "normalize_silent",
              "arguments": {
                "state": {
                  "ref": "steps.compile.outputs.state"
                },
                "context": {
                  "ref": "inputs.context"
                }
              },
              "description": "Overwrite lean_execution.json with no_known_diagnostics and empty findings/counts; change stage payload_status only, retaining the recorded execution ok flag."
            }
          }
        ],
        "default": {
          "kind": "call",
          "operation": "retain_state",
          "arguments": {
            "state": {
              "ref": "steps.compile.outputs.state"
            },
            "context": {
              "ref": "inputs.context"
            }
          },
          "description": "Source-backed MCP state validation/copy preserves nonsilent or failed compilation evidence unchanged."
        },
        "outputs": {
          "state": {
            "type": "State",
            "value": {
              "ref": "selected.outputs.state"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "report",
        "kind": "call",
        "operation": "validate_report",
        "arguments": {
          "state": {
            "ref": "steps.evidence.outputs.state"
          },
          "context": {
            "ref": "inputs.context"
          }
        },
        "description": "Run consistency_report with --compile-ok iff compilation succeeded, --realness-ok iff also lean_execution payload_status=no_known_diagnostics, and unconditional --anchor-ok; then review_refinement_plan. Rebuild/write source_record.rebuilt.json; run derivation_completeness with recursive-frontier-count=0, then case_thoroughness. Write recursive_goal_case_run.json with all stage reports, acceptance, source/Lean/artifact paths and formal_answer_policy; print as requested. Main returns result.returncode."
      }
    ],
    "outputs": {
      "result": {
        "type": "RunResult",
        "value": {
          "ref": "steps.report.outputs.result"
        }
      }
    }
  },
